A||N||12||myblack86GT||Mr. Mikes Leather Seats||||1||
Z||000000||myblack86GT||09-04-2000||08:30 AM||||I am going to buy some. I was just wondering: Are they really as easy to install as he says they are? (3 hours first one, 1 hour for the second) Are they good quality leather? And is he easy to deal with (help and installation problems). Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||09-04-2000||10:32 AM||||It took me about 1 hour 10 minutes for the first seat and just under an hour for the second seat. The video he gives you is VERY well done, easy to follow, and he explains every step carefully. He also gives you EVERYTHING to do the seats. Quality is excellent. If you have any questions he's more than willing to take time to answer them.<BR>Highly Recommended!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||myblack86GT||09-04-2000||11:34 AM||||Ok, Thanks, all I needed to know. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Robert||09-04-2000||09:51 PM||||"It took me about 1 hour 10 minutes"   <P>WOW!!! Oreif....  That is fast.  Took over 3 hours for me to do the first seat, about half that for the second. But.....I was working in my living room with one hand on the VCR rewind button.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||09-04-2000||10:30 PM||||The trick is to watch the video first. Then rewind it and start on the seats. If you need to review just hit FF and then play.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ed||09-05-2000||01:15 AM||||I had a good experience also.  But I also took the longer time.  When they were done they looked as if they were done professionally.  <P>I also watched and replayed the video as I went along.  <P>I recommend them.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||09-05-2000||02:44 PM||||Well I don't have leather YET!! but a very nice forum member sold me his very, very, near mint stock covers when he got leathers <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>he also sent the Mr. mikes video, hog rings and tool. (THANKS) they went on smooth, about 1hr. per seat. I watched the video first and then did the seats.<P>DXR_DAD ||||reg||14
Z||000007||Boomtastic||09-05-2000||10:12 PM||||I watched the video - all 25 minutes of it - and said "Phew - piece of cake!" 3 hours later, my first seat was done. It was those damn vertical bars I tell ya - they'll get ya everytime!! I swore it wouldn't take me as long on the other seat, and by gum I was right. 2 hours for the passenger seat, and I had some of the nicest leathers around.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> But seriously, despite the time (which, when you think about it, shows the amount of quality *you* put into your finished product), Mike provides everything you need to do the job except a black magic marker, and even that really isn't needed. Hog rings, hog ring pliers, foam, spray adhesive (some of the best I've ever seen!!), cotton for the bolsters .. heck, even razor blades! You cannot go wrong with this kit. Sure I sweat my arse off installing them, but the finished product is well worth it.<P>Oh yeah - I almost forgot! Not all of the seat is leather. Only the part that you actually sit on is leather, which while it sounds like a rip off, if I didn't tell you then you would never know. The vinyl is such a perfect match that it blends seamlessly with the rest of the seat. I encourage you to visit Mikes web page (http://www.mrmikes.com) and order yourself a sample copy of the leathers. This will give you an idea of the leather he uses, as well as an idea of what color you would like to make the seats in.<p>[This message has been edited by Boomtastic (edited 09-05-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000008||Oreif||09-05-2000||11:04 PM||||Vertical bars? Oh maybe the time is dependant on the style of seat you order. I have the "380" style. With the logo and stripe. I don't know if the seats with the vertical stripes are different to do. That might explain the difference in time.||||reg||4
Z||000009||Monkeyman||09-05-2000||11:16 PM||||I think he meant the metal bars attached to the seat (never seen 'em in person, just in pics).  I plan on one of the 410 series.  Maybe the gathered leather look.  Who knows.  <P>The material that is not leather is a very good quality vinyl.  Mike could probably make the entire seat out of that and you wouldn't know the difference.  (heh heh--maybe he does----J/K)||||reg||1
Z||000010||MikeSchaefer||09-06-2000||12:30 AM||||Mike is the man!  Definately do it, even if it takes you 10 hours (which it won't) they're worth every minute you spend putting them in.  I have style 430 and love them to death.  I think I spent around 3 for the first and about 2 for the second.  Definately watch the video first like Robert said, then FF and Pause your way through it!<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> <BR>p.s. within a week I'll have pics up on my page.  Black with lobster red centers<p>[This message has been edited by MikeSchaefer (edited 09-06-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000011||Fret Naught||09-06-2000||03:11 PM||||Mr. Mike is my Hero,<BR>When it is all said and done, I think that you get more than pay for.||||reg||14
Z||000012||Carrolles||09-06-2000||05:25 PM||||Just about every car I look at that has leather seats has leather only on the seating surfaces.  The rest is covered in vinyl.||||reg||1
